    {
      "moduleNumber": "M23",
      "pillar": "P08",
      "pillarName": "Architecture & Patterns",
      "moduleSlug": "frontend-architecture",
      "title": "Frontend Architecture & Patterns",
      "appUrl": "/frontend-intermediate/frontend-architecture",
      "seoSlug": "frontend-architecture-interview-questions",
      "seoUrl": "/frontend-architecture-interview-questions",
      "altSlugs": [
        "micro-frontend-interview-questions",
        "design-system-architecture-questions"
      ],
      "altUrls": [
        "/micro-frontend-interview-questions",
        "/design-system-architecture-questions"
      ],
      "topics": [
        "micro-frontends",
        "module-federation",
        "design-systems-architecture",
        "component-architecture-patterns",
        "monorepo-frontend",
        "frontend-ddd"
      ],
      "intro": "Frontend architecture questions are asked at senior/staff frontend interviews and increasingly at mid-level. Interviewers probe: when would you choose a micro-frontend architecture over a monolith? How does Webpack Module Federation work and what problem does it solve? What makes a design system different from a component library? How do you structure a large React or Angular application so teams can work independently without stepping on each other? How does a monorepo tool (Nx, Turborepo) help and what trade-offs does it introduce? This module gives you the vocabulary, trade-offs, and decision frameworks to answer these questions without hedging."
    },
    {
      "moduleNumber": "M24",
      "pillar": "P09",
      "pillarName": "Application Security",
      "moduleSlug": "frontend-security",
      "title": "Web Security for Frontend Engineers",
      "appUrl": "/frontend-intermediate/frontend-security",
      "seoSlug": "frontend-security-interview-questions",
      "seoUrl": "/frontend-security-interview-questions",
      "altSlugs": [
        "web-security-frontend-interview",
        "xss-csrf-interview-questions"
      ],
      "altUrls": [
        "/web-security-frontend-interview",
        "/xss-csrf-interview-questions"
      ],
      "topics": [
        "xss-prevention-frontend",
        "csrf-protection",
        "csp-headers",
        "secure-token-storage",
        "cors-from-frontend",
        "oauth-pkce-flow"
      ],
      "intro": "Web security questions appear in mid-to-senior frontend interviews at companies that care about production quality. The core topics: XSS (reflected, stored, DOM-based \u2014 why React's JSX escapes by default but dangerouslySetInnerHTML does not), CSRF (the attack flow and why SameSite=Strict or SameSite=Lax cookies prevent it), Content Security Policy headers and what a policy like default-src 'self' actually blocks, the localStorage vs httpOnly cookie debate for storing JWTs (the correct answer: httpOnly cookie, and why), CORS pre-flight mechanics (why the browser sends OPTIONS first and what the server must respond), and the OAuth 2.0 PKCE flow for SPAs (why the implicit flow is deprecated and what PKCE replaces it with)."
    },
    {
      "moduleNumber": "M25",
      "pillar": "P10",
      "pillarName": "System Design",
      "moduleSlug": "frontend-system-design",
      "title": "Frontend System Design",
      "appUrl": "/frontend-intermediate/frontend-system-design",
      "seoSlug": "frontend-system-design-interview-questions",
      "seoUrl": "/frontend-system-design-interview-questions",
      "altSlugs": [
        "frontend-system-design-problems",
        "ui-system-design-interview"
      ],
      "altUrls": [
        "/frontend-system-design-problems",
        "/ui-system-design-interview"
      ],
      "topics": [
        "infinite-scroll-design",
        "real-time-feed",
        "search-autocomplete-frontend",
        "virtual-list",
        "image-cdn-optimization",
        "design-system-component-library"
      ],
      "intro": "Frontend system design is now a dedicated interview round at FAANG-adjacent and growth-stage companies. The format: \"design an infinite scroll news feed\" or \"design the search autocomplete for Amazon\" in 45 minutes \u2014 you are expected to think through component tree, data fetching strategy, state management, performance, and edge cases. This module walks through six canonical frontend system design problems: infinite scroll (cursor vs offset pagination, IntersectionObserver, prefetch), real-time feed (WebSocket vs SSE vs long-polling trade-offs), search autocomplete (debounce, caching, cancellation), virtual list / windowing (why DOM nodes are expensive, how react-window works), image CDN optimization (lazy loading, format selection, responsive srcset), and design system architecture (token system, theming, component API design)."
    },
    {
      "moduleNumber": "M26",
      "pillar": "P11",
      "pillarName": "Engineering Practices",
      "moduleSlug": "engineering-practices-fe",
