      ],
      "topics": [
        "code-review-frontend",
        "accessibility-a11y",
        "performance-budgets",
        "monorepo-tools-workflow",
        "engineering-culture-fe"
      ],
      "intro": "Engineering practices questions appear at staff and senior frontend interviews: \"how do you run a code review for a 500-line React PR?\", \"how do you enforce accessibility in a large design system?\", \"what Core Web Vitals do you track and how?\", \"how does your team manage a monorepo with 30 packages?\". This module covers code review standards specific to frontend (visual regression, accessibility, bundle impact, semantic HTML), how to bake a11y into a component library from day one (ARIA roles, focus management, screen-reader testing), performance budgets (setting Lighthouse thresholds in CI, LCP/FID/CLS targets), and the engineering culture questions that distinguish senior contributors from senior coders."
    }
  ]
